13.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2}

B2 is the vital point that severs Black's shape while immediately threatening the disconnected C1-C2 stones. It forces Black into a shortage of liberties regardless of reply: if Black tries to capture at B1, White can follow up by tightening around A3/A4 to prevent two eyes; if Black ignores or plays elsewhere (A1, A3, A4), White exploits the atari on C1-C2 or wedges further at B1 to finish the capture. 

By contrast, starting at B1 lets Black answer at B2, connecting everything into one group with eye potential at A1 and A3. From there Black can answer any follow-up (such as A4 or A3) by capturing the B1 stone or securing the remaining liberties, resulting in life. Moves like A3 or C5 are too loose and allow Black the same connecting reply at B2. Thus only B2 initiates a forcing kill sequence that works against all Black defenses.

