14.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2}

B2 remains the only first move that reliably initiates a kill regardless of Black's replies. It occupies the shared connection point between the disconnected C1-C2 pair and the A2-B3-B4 cluster, immediately creating a multi-group shortage of liberties. Black must answer locally; any attempt to capture at B1 leaves the combined shape with only A1/A3/A4 as potential liberties, and White can then tighten at A3 or C5 to eliminate real eye space along the edge before Black stabilizes. If Black ignores or plays A1/A3/A4 first, White exploits the atari on C1-C2 or wedges further to finish the capture.

By contrast, the detailed B1 lines still contain gaps after the proposed A4 follow-up. When Black responds to A4 by capturing at A1, the newly opened B1 point becomes an internal liberty that Black can later fill safely once White commits to A3, turning the corner into a living false-eye shape rather than a forced capture. This leaves Black with a viable defense that the B1 sequences have not fully closed. Moves like A3 or C5 are too slow and permit Black to occupy B2 first, connecting everything into a living group. Thus only B2 forces the kill against every possible Black defense.

